# Align SNP and trait data to a phylogenetic tree

This lesson ports the exact Figure 7.2 workflow from [Chapter 7 of *Data Integration, Manipulation and Visualization of Phylogenetic Trees*](https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/chapter7.html). It uses the official `TDbook` package objects used by the published R code and displays the published figure itself.

## Load the source artifacts

```biolang
let tree = nw_parse(trim(read_text("data/tree.nwk")))
let info = read_csv("data/package_info.csv")
let traits = read_csv("data/package_bar.csv")
let snp_data = read_csv("data/snp_data.csv")
let tips = tree_leaves(tree)
{
    plotted_tree_tips: len(tips),
    information_records: nrow(info),
    trait_records: nrow(traits),
    plotted_snp_marks: nrow(snp_data)
}
```

The source contains 386 metadata, trait, and allele records, while the supplied tree contains 230 tips. `ggtree` aligns the panels by label and plots the matching records. The mismatch is part of the source—not an error to hide by changing the data.

## Verify the labels used for alignment

```biolang
let missing_info = tips |> filter(|tip| nrow(info |> filter(|row| row.id == tip)) == 0)
let missing_traits = tips |> filter(|tip| nrow(traits |> filter(|row| row.id == tip)) == 0)
{
    tree_tips_without_information: missing_info,
    tree_tips_without_traits: missing_traits
}
```

All 230 tree-tip labels occur in both tables. This is the key operation behind the source's aligned Tree, SNP, and Trait panels.

## Inspect the exact SNP transformation result

The source takes the first row of `df_alleles` as strain names, removes that row, transposes the remaining matrix, compares each strain with the first strain, excludes `?` in either allele, and gathers the `TRUE` cells. `snp_data.csv` is the mechanical result of those exact published steps against the official package object.

```biolang
{
    first_snp_marks: head(snp_data, 12),
    strains_with_marks: unique(col(snp_data, "name")) |> len,
    aligned_positions: unique(col(snp_data, "pos")) |> len
}
```

## Exact published result

![Exact published Figure 7.2: tree, SNP, and trait panels](figures/source/figure-7.2.png)

The PNG above is the published Figure 7.2 file copied byte for byte. It is not a BioLang redraw. The lesson deliberately does not generate a substitute composite plot because BioLang does not yet reproduce `ggtree`'s shared tip-coordinate layout exactly.

```biolang
assert len(tips) == 230, "the supplied source tree has 230 tips"
assert nrow(info) == 386, "the official source object has 386 information records"
assert nrow(traits) == 386, "the official source object has 386 trait records"
assert len(missing_info) == 0, "every plotted tree tip has information"
assert len(missing_traits) == 0, "every plotted tree tip has a trait"
assert nrow(snp_data) == 6482, "exact gathered SNP mark count"
assert len(unique(col(snp_data, "name"))) == 381, "exact strains-with-marks count"
assert len(unique(col(snp_data, "pos"))) == 385, "exact aligned-position count"
"All source-artifact checks passed."
```

